{
  "id": "maximum_average_subarray_i",
  "title": "Maximum Average Subarray I",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Sliding Window"
  ],
  "description": "<p>You are given an integer array <code>nums</code> consisting of <code>n</code> elements, and an integer <code>k</code>.</p> <p>Find a contiguous subarray whose <strong>length is equal to</strong> <code>k</code> that has the maximum average value and return <em>this value</em>. Any answer with a calculation error less than <code>10<sup>-5</sup></code> will be accepted.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,12,-5,-6,50,3], k = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> 12.75000\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Maximum average is (12 - 5 - 6 + 50) / 4 = 51 / 4 = 12.75\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [5], k = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 5.00000\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>n == nums.length</code></li> <li><code>1 &lt;= k &lt;= n &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li> <li><code>-10<sup>4</sup> &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "findMaxAverage",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "type": "array"
      },
      {
        "name": "k",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ]
  },
